' ============================================================================
' BULLET - Projectile fired by the player's gun
' Converted from official Godot 2D Platformer demo
' ============================================================================
' Attached to a RigidBody2D node in bullet.tscn.
' The bullet flies until it hits something (via contact_monitor).
' On contact with an enemy, it calls destroy() on the enemy.
' A Timer in the scene auto-destroys bullets after a timeout.
'
' Note: The original GDScript used "body is Enemy" type checking.
' Since VG doesn't support class_name type checks, we use Godot's
' group system instead: enemies are in the "enemies" group.
' ============================================================================
Attribute VB_Name = "Bullet"

' --- Node references ---
Dim animPlayer As Object        ' AnimationPlayer - destroy animation

' ============================================================================
' INITIALIZATION
' ============================================================================
Sub _Ready()
    animPlayer = GetNode("AnimationPlayer")
End Sub

' ============================================================================
' SELF-DESTRUCT - Play destroy animation then queue_free (via animation)
' ============================================================================
' Called by the Timer timeout signal and can be called externally.
' The "destroy" animation in the scene ends with a queue_free() method track.
Sub destroy()
    animPlayer.Play("destroy")
End Sub

' ============================================================================
' COLLISION HANDLER - Called when bullet contacts a physics body
' ============================================================================
' Connected via signal in bullet.tscn:
'   [connection signal="body_entered" from="." to="." method="_on_body_entered"]
'
' VG's call_internal uses case-insensitive matching, so this Sub name
' matches the snake_case method name in the .tscn signal connection.
Sub _on_body_entered(body As Object)
    ' Check if the body is an enemy using Godot's group system
    ' (replaces "body is Enemy" type check from GDScript)
    If body.IsInGroup("enemies") Then
        ' Call the enemy's destroy method
        body.destroy()
    End If
End Sub
